description:
Purpose: prove that the production path can turn an immutable preseason checkpoint into a complete advisory starting-squad decision before the final GW1 deadline.

Use T-48h as the fixed rehearsal input. If T-48h was not successfully captured, the rehearsal is a no-go; do not substitute a later checkpoint. Execute capture verification -> evidence assembly/retrieval -> deterministic forecast -> initial-15 optimiser -> validation -> frozen Gameweek Decision Record (GDR). Then repeat the unchanged request to prove determinism. After the final checkpoint exists, compare it with the rehearsal without revising the earlier artifact.

Persist under evals/live-readiness/2026-27-gw1/:
- input manifest and hashes;
- source/family coverage and quarantine summary;
- stage timings and peak memory where available;
- candidate/evidence packet hashes;
- recommendation and GDR;
- validation, degraded-mode and go/no decisions;
- unchanged-input rerun comparison;
- later final-checkpoint comparison.

Default go/no gates:
- all manifest and predecessor hashes verify;
- mandatory official bootstrap, fixtures and ruleset are admitted;
- zero temporal-leakage, schema, identity, legality or artifact-integrity errors;
- rerun immutable artifacts are byte-identical;
- every optional feed failure is explicitly degraded;
- total rehearsal wall time is at most 30 minutes on the recorded host, and the deterministic forecast-plus-optimiser fallback completes within 10 minutes;
- no live-account write mechanism is loaded or invoked.

Files:
- docs/execplans/fpl-jm0-live-readiness-rehearsal.md
- evals/live-readiness/2026-27-gw1/
- scripts/run_live_readiness_rehearsal.py
- tests/integration/test_live_readiness_rehearsal.py
- docs/evaluation/2026-27-gw1-live-readiness.md

Required CLI:
python scripts/run_live_readiness_rehearsal.py --checkpoint T-48h --manifest <path> --output-root evals/live-readiness/2026-27-gw1

Non-goals: retrospective points claims, changing the earlier recommendation after final data, policy promotion, or submitting a team.
